Automated EC2 Health Monitoring & Slack Alerts 
I was spending too much time checking EC2 servers manually.
While managing multiple EC2 instances, I kept checking the same things again and again:

Running / Stopped state, 1/2 Status Checks, CPU usage, Memory usage,
At one point I thought:
Why am I checking all of this manually every time?
So I decided to automate it.
I built a simple flow:

EventBridge → Lambda → EC2 / CloudWatch / SSM → Slack
Every 5 minutes, Lambda checks the EC2 instances.
If something goes wrong, I get a Slack alert with the affected server details.
Now I don't have to check every server manually. I can see the issue quickly and start troubleshooting.
Less manual checking. Faster alerts. Quicker troubleshooting.
Has anyone else faced the same problem?
How did you handle it?
